-- title:
--   Lemma 3.13 — an explicit efficiently encodable $[\![7^v,1,3^v]\!]$ positive-sign CSS code family
-- statement:
--   For every integer $v\ge1$ there is a positive-sign CSS code on $N=7^v$ qubits, with $X$-check space $S_X^{(v)}$ and $Z$-check space $S_Z^{(v)}$, such that:
--
--   1. **parameters $[\![7^v,1,3^v]\!]$:** the generated group is a stabilizer group, the codespace has dimension $2^1$, and the code distance (Definition 3.8) is exactly $3^v$;
--   2. **efficiently encodable:** an encoder circuit over Clifford+T, whose description is computed from $1^{7^v}$ in polynomial time, maps $|b\rangle$ on its input wire (all other wires $|0\rangle$) to orthonormal codewords $|b_L\rangle$ in the codespace;
--   3. **logical Paulis:** $X^{\otimes7^v}|b_L\rangle=|(1-b)_L\rangle$ and $Z^{\otimes7^v}|b_L\rangle=(-1)^b|b_L\rangle$;
--   4. **transversal logical CNOT:** $\mathrm{CNOT}^{\otimes7^v}|a_L\rangle|b_L\rangle=|a_L\rangle|(a\oplus b)_L\rangle$;
--   5. **strict checks:** the strict $Z$- and $X$-basis measurement decoders (reject every nonzero syndrome, else output the logical parity) are computable in time polynomial in the block length.
--
--   This is the inner code of the trap-code authentication; level $v=\lceil\log_3\mu^3\rceil$ gives distance at least $\mu^3$ with block length below $7\mu^6$ (488).
--
--   **Formalization Note** The stabilizer group, codespace, normalizer, phase-discarded group and Pauli weight are those of the published stabilizer layer. "Polynomial time" is polynomial in the block length $7^v$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: "efficiently encodable" → an encoder Layered circuit on 7^v wires with an input wire, produced from unary(7^v) by a PolyTimeComputable map, whose outputs on |b⟩|0…0⟩ are the logical basis states; reason: the proof's "Recursive encoding … take polynomial time", polynomial in the block length
--   - encoding: "strict X- and Z-basis measurement checks are computable in polynomial time" → strictDecZ / strictDecX (reject unless every check is satisfied, else the logical parity) computed by PolyTimeComputable maps on ⟨1^v, c⟩; reason: Definition 3.10 with the strict check of the proof ("rejects every nonzero syndrome")
--   - encoding: "logical X, Z represented by X^{⊗7^v} and Z^{⊗7^v}", "transversal logical CNOT" → the action of X^{⊗N}, Z^{⊗N} and CNOT^{⊗N} on the encoder's logical basis |b_L⟩; reason: logical operators are defined by their action on a logical basis
--   - encoding: ⟦7^v, 1, 3^v⟧ (Definitions 3.7, 3.8) → IsStabilizerGroup, finrank of stabilizedSpace = 2^1, and IsLeast of the distance set = 3^v, with the published stabilizer layer; reason: the definitions of pp.19–20
-- source:
--   Chung, Cojocaru, Lee, Lin, Classical Verification of Quantum Sampling with Negligible Error, STOC 2027 submission (held version, sha256 dbc19d8f…7ee7), Lemma 3.13, p.21 (PDF 22); Definitions 3.7, 3.8, 3.10, pp.19–20 (PDF 20–21)

import Definitions.Def_QSampVerif_cssGroup

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace QSampVerif

open QAlgorithms QAlgorithms.Complexity QAlgorithms.Stabilizer

/-- Chung, Cojocaru, Lee, Lin, STOC 2027 submission (held version, sha256 dbc19d8f…7ee7),
Lemma 3.13 (An explicit code family), p.21 (PDF 22), with Definitions 3.7, 3.8 and 3.10
(pp.19–20).

For every `v ≥ 1` there is a positive-sign CSS code on `7^v` qubits (stabilizer group generated by
`X^u`, `u ∈ Sx_v`, and `Z^w`, `w ∈ Sz_v`, all with sign `+1`) such that
1. it is a stabilizer code with parameters `⟦7^v, 1, 3^v⟧`: the group is a stabilizer group, the
   codespace has dimension `2^1`, and the distance (Definition 3.8) is exactly `3^v`;
2. it is efficiently encodable: an encoder circuit, produced in time polynomial in the block
   length, maps `|b⟩` on its input wire (all other wires `|0⟩`) to logical basis states
   `|b_L⟩`, which are orthonormal and lie in the codespace;
3. logical `X` and `Z` are represented by `X^{⊗7^v}` and `Z^{⊗7^v}`:
   `X^{⊗7^v}|b_L⟩ = |(1−b)_L⟩` and `Z^{⊗7^v}|b_L⟩ = (−1)^b |b_L⟩`;
4. logical CNOT is transversal: `CNOT^{⊗7^v}|a_L⟩|b_L⟩ = |a_L⟩|(a ⊕ b)_L⟩`;
5. its strict `Z`- and `X`-basis measurement checks (Definition 3.10) are computable in
   polynomial time.

**Formalization Note.** The stabilizer group, codespace, normalizer, phase-discarded group and
weights are the published `QAlgorithms` ones (`IsStabilizerGroup`, `stabilizedSpace`,
`pauliCentralizer`, `phaseMultiples`, `PauliString.weight`). The encoder is a layered circuit over
the published Clifford+T instructions; "polynomial time" is polynomial in the block length `7^v`
(the encoder is produced from `1^{7^v}`, the checks read `⟨1^v, c⟩` with `|c| = 7^v`). -/
theorem lemma_3_13 :
    ∃ (Sx Sz : (v : ℕ) → Submodule (ZMod 2) (Fin (7 ^ v) → ZMod 2))
      (enc : (v : ℕ) → Layered (7 ^ v)) (inWire : (v : ℕ) → Fin (7 ^ v)),
      (∃ f : Str → Str, PolyTimeComputable f ∧ ∀ v : ℕ, 1 ≤ v →
        f (unary (7 ^ v)) = tup [unary (inWire v).val, encCirc (enc v)]) ∧
      (∃ f : Str → Str, PolyTimeComputable f ∧ ∀ v : ℕ, 1 ≤ v → ∀ c : Fin (7 ^ v) → ZMod 2,
        f (tup [unary v, wordStr c]) = encOptBool (strictDecZ (Sz v) c)) ∧
      (∃ f : Str → Str, PolyTimeComputable f ∧ ∀ v : ℕ, 1 ≤ v → ∀ c : Fin (7 ^ v) → ZMod 2,
        f (tup [unary v, wordStr c]) = encOptBool (strictDecX (Sx v) c)) ∧
      ∀ v : ℕ, 1 ≤ v →
        IsStabilizerGroup (cssGroup (Sx v) (Sz v)) ∧
        Module.finrank ℂ (stabilizedSpace (cssGroup (Sx v) (Sz v))) = 2 ^ 1 ∧
        IsLeast (codeDistanceSet (cssGroup (Sx v) (Sz v))) (3 ^ v) ∧
        (∀ b : Bool,
          encodedState (enc v) (inWire v) b ∈ stabilizedSpace (cssGroup (Sx v) (Sz v)) ∧
          ‖encodedState (enc v) (inWire v) b‖ = 1) ∧
        inner ℂ (encodedState (enc v) (inWire v) false) (encodedState (enc v) (inWire v) true) = 0 ∧
        (∀ b : Bool, act (allPauli (7 ^ v) Pauli.X) (encodedState (enc v) (inWire v) b) =
          encodedState (enc v) (inWire v) (!b)) ∧
        (∀ b : Bool, act (allPauli (7 ^ v) Pauli.Z) (encodedState (enc v) (inWire v) b) =
          (if b then (-1 : ℂ) else 1) • encodedState (enc v) (inWire v) b) ∧
        (∀ a b : Bool, act (transversalCNOT (7 ^ v))
            (tensorVec (encodedState (enc v) (inWire v) a) (encodedState (enc v) (inWire v) b)) =
          tensorVec (encodedState (enc v) (inWire v) a)
            (encodedState (enc v) (inWire v) (xor a b))) := by sorry

end QSampVerif
